{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronRegion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronRegion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeMeasure"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.chimney_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.chimney_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronRegion.lean#L120-L127","doc":"A point of the base, lifted high enough, is in the chimney -- so a chimney\nover a nonempty base is nonempty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.chimney_fibre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.chimney_fibre","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronRegion.lean#L104-L113","doc":"**The vertical fibre of a chimney is exactly a ray** -- the shape H4-1\nintegrates.\n\nThis is the bridge between H3 and H4: `integral_Ioi_hemisphere` computes\n`∫ z in Ioi (√(R² − d²)), z⁻³ = 1/(2(R² − d²))`, and this says that ray IS the\nfibre. H4-2 then only has to justify integrating fibrewise (Fubini). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.chimney_subset_upperHalfSpace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.chimney_subset_upperHalfSpace","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronRegion.lean#L92-L102","doc":"**Every chimney sits in the upper half-space** -- with no hypothesis on the\nbase at all.\n\n`Real.sqrt` is non-negative even where its argument is (so outside the disk the\nfloor degenerates to `z > 0`), which is exactly what makes this unconditional.\nThat is a genuine convenience of the `Real.sqrt` convention rather than an\naccident: it means the region never silently escapes `H³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurableSet_chimney","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurableSet_chimney","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronRegion.lean#L80-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurable_baseProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurable_baseProj","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronRegion.lean#L77-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.baseProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.baseProj","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronRegion.lean#L74-L75","doc":"The base-projection map `(x,y,z) ↦ (x,y)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.chimney","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.chimney","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronRegion.lean#L63-L72","doc":"**The solid over a base set, above the hemisphere of radius `R`.**\n\nMilnor's normalized position uses `R = 1`; the radius is left free because it\ncosts nothing and H4-1 (`integral_Ioi_hemisphere`) is already stated at general\n`R`.\n\nThe far vertex sits at infinity, so this is unbounded upward -- a \"chimney\" over\n`T`, not a bounded solid. That product shape is what H4-2's Fubini consumes. ","signatureChunk":0}]}